Setting up a clean FastAPI environment requires python's built-in venv (or uv), installing fastapi along with uvicorn (ASGI server), and organizing a standard project structure.
1. Terminal Commands (Setup & Installation)
Run these commands in your terminal to create your directory, set up a virtual environment, and install dependencies:
# Create project folder and enter it
mkdir fastapi-app
cd fastapi-app

# Create a virtual environment (.venv)
python3 -m venv .venv

# Activate the virtual environment
# On macOS/Linux:
source .venv/bin/activate
# On Windows (PowerShell):
# .venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1

# Upgrade pip and install FastAPI + Uvicorn
pip install --upgrade pip
pip install "fastapi[standard]"

> Tip: Installing fastapi[standard] includes uvicorn, pydantic, email-validator, and python-multipart automatically.
> 
2. Basic Project Structure
Organize your files cleanly from the start:
fastapi-app/
├── .venv/
├── app/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   └── main.py
├── .gitignore
└── requirements.txt

Generate your requirements.txt:
pip freeze > requirements.txt

3. Starter Code (app/main.py)
Create app/main.py and paste the following boilerplate:
from fastapi import FastAPI
from pydantic import BaseModel

app = FastAPI(
    title="My FastAPI App",
    description="Starter setup for FastAPI",
    version="0.1.0"
)

# Example Request Body Schema
class Item(BaseModel):
    name: str
    price: float
    is_offer: bool | None = None

@app.get("/")
def read_root():
    return {"message": "Hello World"}

@app.get("/items/{item_id}")
def read_item(item_id: int, q: str | None = None):
    return {"item_id": item_id, "q": q}

@app.post("/items/")
def create_item(item: Item):
    return {"item_name": item.name, "item_price": item.price}

4. Running the Development Server
From your root directory (fastapi-app/), start the server with hot-reloading:
fastapi dev app/main.py

(Alternatively, using uvicorn directly: uvicorn app.main:app --reload)
Once running, access your API and automated documentation:
 * API Root: [http://127.0.0.1:8000/](http://127.0.0.1:8000/)
 * Interactive Swagger UI: [http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs](http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs)
 * Alternative ReDoc Docs: [http://127.0.0.1:8000/redoc](http://127.0.0.1:8000/redoc)
